  "school": "Price Action",
  "asset": "US 100",
  "timeframe": "1H",
  "market_context": "Uptrend on US 100 Cash CFD during Jan 2025, interrupted by a sharp 6% drop due to DeepSeek AI news. Analyst demonstrates multiple consecutive long entries after break-of-structure (BOS) impulses, each retracing to the 0.5–0.618 Fib gold zone with confirmation candles.",
  "key_observation": "After each impulse move breaking a prior swing high, price consistently retraced to the Fibonacci gold zone (0.5–0.618), where bullish rejection wicks and inside bars formed, enabling high-probability long entries targeting the previous high or Fib extensions.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the most recent break-of-structure (BOS) — a strong nonstop impulse move that closed above the previous swing high.",
    "Step 2: Draw Fibonacci retracement from the low (including wick) of the impulse start to the high (including wick) of the impulse peak.",
    "Step 3: Monitor price retracement into the gold zone (0.5 to 0.618 levels), looking for rejection signals: long bullish wick, inside bar, or engulfing candle.",
    "Step 4: Enter long at the 0.618 level with stop loss below it; set take profit at the prior swing high (TP1), optionally adding partial profits at 0.5 and 1.0 Fib extensions.",
    "Step 5: Repeat the process for the next BOS after price makes a new high, re-measuring the new impulse leg and waiting for retracement to the gold zone."
  ],
  "outcome": "One trade hit stop loss due to DeepSeek news event (6% market drop), but risk was limited by stop placement; another trade showed Closed P&L: 298.41 with R:R 2.56 (frame f013).",
  "lessons": "Fibonacci retracements work best in strong trends after clear BOS; the gold zone (0.5–0.618) is the highest-probability entry area when confirmed by price action (rejection wick, inside bar). Always use stop loss below 0.618 and avoid trading during consolidation.",
